{%- comment -%}
  horizon-blocks Phase 2–9 — UI-layer tokens (z-index ramp + opacity constants;
  Phase 3 appends icon/slideshow/animation constants + primary-button shims;
  Phase 4 appends accordion/menu/social sizes + popover tokens + the
  --color-border fallback; Phase 5 appends the slideshow-controls
  dots/counter sizes; Phase 7 appends the section-height ramp; Phase 8
  appends the fade-in easing; Phase 9 appends the dialog/popup sizes +
  backdrop tokens and the .color-custom-popover scope render; Phase 10
  appends the card slice's tokens — swatch/variant-picker sizes, badge
  paddings, card-hover system, input borders, the color-palette :root
  analogs (--color-foreground-rgb, brightness opacities,
  --color-foreground-subdued, the --color-variant-* family with hover-shift
  math via util-palette-hover-shift) and the .color-custom-badge-sale /
  -sold-out scope renders; Phase 13 appends the quick-add/buy-buttons
  subsystem's tokens — font-size/gap fills, animation timings, button/input
  sizes, drawer + quick-add-modal geometry — and the .color-custom-drawer
  scope render (tsv:693-698 analog of the Phase-9 popover scope).

  Dawn-side equivalent of the layering + opacity subset of stock Horizon
  v4.1.1 (68760d9) snippets/theme-styles-variables.liquid, values verbatim.
  Dawn has no equivalent tokens; the Phase-2 card slice consumes
  --layer-flat / --layer-raised (card content/link stacking) and
  --opacity-* (contrast-override's muted/subdued text + form tokens,
  overlay fallback color). The FULL ramps are emitted, not just the
  consumed subset, so future slices (sticky headers, drawers, popovers)
  reuse this file instead of growing new partial copies.

  Rendered by sections/hz-blocks-host.liquid next to hz-type-variables —
  same ownership precedent; future hosts render both.

  Emitted via {% style %} (Liquid tag) — exempt from Shopify's CSS
  subsetting, so the tokens survive even when no static CSS references them.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # Phase 9: Dawn's closest analog of Horizon's popover color settings
  # (tsv:685-691 feeds contrast-override from settings.popover_* — theme
  # settings Dawn lacks; their schema DEFAULTS are palette background/
  # foreground = exactly Dawn scheme-1's background/text). Same
  # first-scheme access pattern as contrast-override.liquid:86.
  # Scheme-1-only caveat per the --color-border fallback below.
  assign popover_scheme = settings.color_schemes | first

  # --- Phase 10 (card slice) ---
  # Variant-picker palette at Horizon SCHEMA defaults (settings_schema:
  # palette_variant_background = palette background, palette_variant_text /
  # _border = palette foreground; selected_variant background/border =
  # foreground, text = background) mapped onto Dawn scheme-1 background/text
  # per this file's precedent. Hover values mirror color-palette.liquid:99-131
  # WITH THE DEFAULT-COLLAPSED CONDITIONALS: scheme colors have alpha 1 (no
  # transparency branch); variant border (fg) != background (bg) -> border
  # hover = hover-shift(fg); selected border (fg) == selected background (fg)
  # -> border hover = selected hover background.
  assign hz_variant_bg = popover_scheme.settings.background
  assign hz_variant_fg = popover_scheme.settings.text

  # palette_lightest / palette_darkest analogs (color-palette computes them
  # across the whole palette; our palette IS bg+fg).
  assign hz_bg_brightness = hz_variant_bg | color_brightness
  assign hz_fg_brightness = hz_variant_fg | color_brightness
  if hz_bg_brightness > hz_fg_brightness
    assign hz_palette_lightest = hz_variant_bg
    assign hz_palette_darkest = hz_variant_fg
  else
    assign hz_palette_lightest = hz_variant_fg
    assign hz_palette_darkest = hz_variant_bg
  endif

  capture hz_variant_hover_bg
    render 'util-palette-hover-shift', color: hz_variant_bg
  endcapture
  assign hz_variant_hover_bg = hz_variant_hover_bg | strip
  assign hz_vh_brightness = hz_variant_hover_bg | color_brightness
  if hz_vh_brightness > 128
    assign hz_variant_hover_text = hz_palette_darkest
  else
    assign hz_variant_hover_text = hz_palette_lightest
  endif
  capture hz_variant_hover_border
    render 'util-palette-hover-shift', color: hz_variant_fg
  endcapture
  assign hz_variant_hover_border = hz_variant_hover_border | strip

  capture hz_selected_hover_bg
    render 'util-palette-hover-shift', color: hz_variant_fg
  endcapture
  assign hz_selected_hover_bg = hz_selected_hover_bg | strip
  assign hz_svh_brightness = hz_selected_hover_bg | color_brightness
  if hz_svh_brightness > 128
    assign hz_selected_hover_text = hz_palette_darkest
  else
    assign hz_selected_hover_text = hz_palette_lightest
  endif
  assign hz_selected_hover_border = hz_selected_hover_bg
-%}

{% style %}
  :root {
    /** Z-Index / Layering */
    --layer-section-background: -2;
    --layer-lowest: -1;
    --layer-base: 0;
    --layer-flat: 1;
    --layer-raised: 2;
    --layer-heightened: 4;
    --layer-sticky: 8;
    --layer-window-overlay: 10;
    --layer-header-menu: 12;
    --layer-overlay: 16;
    --layer-menu-drawer: 18;
    --layer-temporary: 20;

    /* Opacity */
    --opacity-5: 0.05;
    --opacity-8: 0.08;
    --opacity-10: 0.1;
    --opacity-15: 0.15;
    --opacity-20: 0.2;
    --opacity-25: 0.25;
    --opacity-30: 0.3;
    --opacity-40: 0.4;
    --opacity-50: 0.5;
    --opacity-60: 0.6;
    --opacity-70: 0.7;
    --opacity-80: 0.8;
    --opacity-85: 0.85;
    --opacity-90: 0.9;
    --opacity-subdued-text: 0.8;
    --opacity-muted-text: 0.6;

    /* --- Phase 3 (carousel slice) --- */
    /* Icons (theme-styles-variables:552 — Horizon icon_stroke setting default) */
    --icon-stroke-width: 1.5px;

    /* Constants (tsv:377-378, 637) */
    --color-white: #ffffff;
    --color-white-rgb: 255 255 255;
    --minimum-touch-target: 44px;

    /* Slideshow sizes (tsv:631-632; Horizon rem = 16px) */
    --slideshow-controls-icon: 32px; /* 2rem */
    --peek-next-slide-size: 48px; /* 3rem */

    /* Padding (tsv:424; 0.7rem) */
    --padding-sm: 11.2px;

    /* Animation (tsv:477, 480) — full ramp per this file's precedent */
    --animation-speed-fast: 0.0625s;
    --animation-speed: 0.125s;
    --animation-speed-medium: 0.15s;
    --animation-speed-slow: 0.2s;
    --animation-easing: ease-in-out;

    /* Primary button colors (Horizon snippets/color-palette.liquid:180-181,
       fed there by theme settings). Dawn mapping shim: deliberate comma-triplet
       composition at the shim boundary — Dawn's --color-button is a comma
       triplet consumed via rgba()/rgb(). Consumed by the circle/square arrow
       shapes; without this they render transparent (IACVT). */
    --color-primary-button-background: rgba(var(--color-button), var(--alpha-button-background));
    --color-primary-button-text: rgb(var(--color-button-text));

    /* --- Phase 4 (accordion + footer leaves; Horizon rem = 16px) --- */
    --margin-xs: 8px; /* tsv:408; 0.5rem — accordion row icon end-margin */
    --style-border-width: 1px; /* tsv:452 — accordion + menu dividers */
    --gap-sm: 11.2px; /* tsv:437; 0.7rem — social-links icon gap */
    --icon-size-xs: 13.6px; /* tsv:548; 0.85rem — summary caret/plus size */
    --icon-size-lg: 24px; /* tsv:551; 1.5rem — social icons */
    --ease-out-quad: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1); /* tsv:474 — popover */

    /* Popover tokens, hardcoded at Horizon SCHEMA defaults (settings-driven
       in stock: tsv:465 reads popover_border_radius, schema default 8 — the
       shipped settings_data.json uses 14, but this token layer's precedent
       is schema defaults, per hz-type-variables). Shadow formula:
       color-palette.liquid:229 with popover_shadow_color at its default
       (= palette foreground); comma-triplet composition at the shim
       boundary like the primary-button colors above. */
    --style-border-radius-popover: 8px;
    --shadow-popover: 0px 4px 20px rgba(var(--color-foreground), var(--opacity-15));

    /* Divider/border fallback (color-palette.liquid:172: --color-border =
       page text color, full strength; Dawn never reads this name — safe at
       :root). Same :root composition caveat as the button shim: resolves
       against the DEFAULT Dawn scheme. Inside .color-custom-* scopes the
       ported contrast-override re-declares it (full-color Horizon model),
       and the accordion's inline divider_color overrides both. */
    --color-border: rgb(var(--color-foreground));

    /* --- Phase 5 (hero slideshow slice; Horizon rem = 16px) --- */
    --padding-lg: 16px; /* tsv:426; 1rem — dots pill inline padding */
    --margin-sm: 11.2px; /* tsv:409; 0.7rem — counter pill inline margin */
    --icon-size-sm: 20px; /* tsv:549; 1.25rem — slideshow-controls icon width */
    --font-size--xs: 13px; /* tsv:351; 0.8125rem — counter text */

    /* --- Phase 7 (layered hero slice) --- */
    /* Section heights (tsv:138-151) — base tier rem→px (Horizon rem = 16px:
       15/25/35rem); the svh tiers below are verbatim (svh needs no
       conversion). Consumed by hz-layered-slideshow's
       --layered-min-height-desktop; token-layer placement matches Horizon's
       own source location, reusable by future sections. */
    --section-height-small: 240px;
    --section-height-medium: 400px;
    --section-height-large: 560px;

    /* --- Phase 8 (utility sweep) --- */
    /* Fade-in easing (tsv:491, verbatim) — jumbo-text blur/reveal transitions */
    --animation-timing-fade-in: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);

    /* Video / deferred-media (consumed by snippets/video.liquid's ported
       support rules). Shadow verbatim (tsv:402); focus outline width
       0.09375rem → 1.5px (tsv:531, Horizon rem = 16px), offset em verbatim
       (tsv:532); button size aliases the Phase-3 touch target (tsv:583). */
    --shadow-button: 0 2px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 20%);
    --focus-outline-width: 1.5px;
    --focus-outline-offset: 0.2em;
    --button-size: var(--minimum-touch-target);

    /* --- Phase 9 (popup-link + dialog primitive; Horizon rem = 16px) --- */
    --padding-xl: 20px; /* tsv:427; 1.25rem */
    --padding-4xl: 32px; /* tsv:430; 2rem */
    --padding-5xl: 48px; /* tsv:431; 3rem */
    --padding-md: 12.8px; /* tsv:425; 0.8rem — dialog-modal mobile padding */
    --margin-2xs: 4.8px; /* tsv:407; 0.3rem — close-button offsets, trigger icon nudge */
    --margin-lg: 16px; /* tsv:411; 1rem — close-button default offsets */
    --normal-content-width: 672px; /* tsv:131; 42rem — modal max-width */
    --modal-max-height: 65dvh; /* tsv:665, verbatim */
    --sidebar-width: 400px; /* tsv:128; 25rem — drawer width */
    --backdrop-opacity: 0.15; /* tsv:635, verbatim */

    /* Popover border, hardcoded at Horizon SCHEMA defaults like the
       Phase-4 popover tokens above (settings-driven in stock: tsv:466
       reads popover_border_width [default 0] + popover_border_color
       [default = palette foreground]). Comma-triplet composition at the
       shim boundary per the --color-border precedent — resolves against
       the DEFAULT Dawn scheme; contrast-override re-declares
       --color-foreground full-color inside .color-custom-* scopes. */
    --style-border-popover: 0px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground));

    /* --- Phase 10 (card slice; Horizon rem = 16px) --- */
    /* Paddings (tsv:428-429) */
    --padding-2xl: 24px; /* 1.5rem */
    --padding-3xl: 28px; /* 1.75rem */

    /* Font sizes (tsv:354-357) */
    --font-size--lg: 18px; /* 1.125rem */
    --font-size--xl: 20px; /* 1.25rem */
    --font-size--2xl: 24px; /* 1.5rem */
    --font-size--3xl: 32px; /* 2rem */

    /* Icons (tsv:547) */
    --icon-size-2xs: 9.6px; /* 0.6rem */

    /* Inputs (tsv:459, 464 — schema defaults inputs_border_radius 8 /
       input_border_width 1) */
    --style-border-width-inputs: 1px;
    --style-border-radius-inputs: 8px;

    /* Swatches (tsv:468-470 + 614-622 — schema defaults
       variant_swatch_* 30/30/100/solid/1/10%) */
    --style-border-swatch-opacity: 10%;
    --style-border-swatch-width: 1px;
    --style-border-swatch-style: solid;
    --variant-picker-swatch-width-unitless: 30;
    --variant-picker-swatch-height-unitless: 30;
    --variant-picker-swatch-width: 30px;
    --variant-picker-swatch-height: 30px;
    --variant-picker-swatch-radius: 100px;
    --variant-picker-border-width: 1px;
    --variant-picker-border-style: solid;
    --variant-picker-border-opacity: 10%;

    /* Variant-picker buttons (tsv:625-626 — schema defaults
       variant_button_radius 8 / variant_button_border_width 1) */
    --variant-picker-button-radius: 8px;
    --variant-picker-button-border-width: 1px;

    /* Badge paddings (tsv:535-543; the responsive tier is re-declared in
       the 750px media block below — this file's section-height precedent) */
    --badge-blob-padding-block: 1px;
    --badge-blob-padding-inline: 12px 8px;
    --badge-rectangle-padding-block: 1px;
    --badge-rectangle-padding-inline: 6px;

    /* Card image sizes (tsv:651-661; rem->px @16, responsive tier below) */
    --card-width-small: 160px; /* 10rem */
    --height-small: 160px; /* 10rem */
    --height-medium: 184px; /* 11.5rem */
    --height-large: 208px; /* 13rem */
    --height-full: 100vh;

    /* Card hover system (Horizon base.css:16-21 — that file's :root is the
       token source for these, not tsv). --hover-shadow-color is composed
       through rgb() because Dawn's --color-shadow is a COMMA triplet
       (dual-format gotcha; rgb(r,g,b) legacy syntax accepts it) —
       consumer-less in the ported subset but kept for fidelity. */
    --hover-lift-amount: 4px;
    --hover-scale-amount: 1.03;
    --hover-subtle-zoom-amount: 1.015;
    --hover-shadow-color: rgb(var(--color-shadow));
    --hover-transition-duration: 0.25s;
    --hover-transition-timing: ease-out;

    /* --- Phase 10 rider (email-signup) --- */
    --gap-xs: 8px; /* tsv:436; 0.5rem */
    --animation-values: var(--animation-speed) var(--animation-easing); /* tsv:484, verbatim */
    /* tsv:593-594 read settings.button_text_case_primary/_secondary (schema
       default "default" — an invalid text-transform value stock lets fall
       through; `none` is the same computed outcome). */
    --button-text-case-primary: none;
    --button-text-case-secondary: none;

    /* Input palette (color-palette:195-198 at schema defaults: input
       background = palette background, text/border = palette foreground).
       -rgb = SPACE triplet per the --color-foreground-rgb note below. */
    --color-input-background: rgb({{ popover_scheme.settings.background.rgb }});
    --color-input-text: rgb({{ popover_scheme.settings.text.rgb }});
    --color-input-text-rgb: {{ popover_scheme.settings.text.rgb }};
    --color-input-border: rgb({{ popover_scheme.settings.text.rgb }});

    /* Palette extremes (color-palette:176-179; computed in the Phase-10
       liquid block above — resolve-custom-hover emits var() references to
       these). */
    --palette-lightest: rgb({{ hz_palette_lightest.rgb }});
    --palette-lightest-rgb: {{ hz_palette_lightest.rgb }};
    --palette-darkest: rgb({{ hz_palette_darkest.rgb }});
    --palette-darkest-rgb: {{ hz_palette_darkest.rgb }};

    /* color-palette.liquid :root analogs from scheme-1 (same scheme-1-only
       caveat as --color-border above). --color-foreground-rgb is a SPACE
       triplet (Horizon convention — consumed via rgb(var() / alpha) slash
       syntax; never feed it to Dawn's comma-triplet rgba() pattern). */
    --color-foreground-rgb: {{ popover_scheme.settings.text.rgb }};
    {% render 'brightness-opacities', background: popover_scheme.settings.background %}
    --color-foreground-subdued: rgb(var(--color-rgb, var(--color-foreground-rgb)) / var(--opacity-subdued-text));

    /* Variant-picker colors (color-palette.liquid:200-213 at schema
       defaults — see the Phase-10 liquid block above for the hover-shift
       derivation). Format deviation from stock's rgb(<rgba>): Dawn scheme
       colors carry no alpha, so the verified .rgb SPACE triplet is composed
       via rgb() instead — identical computed value at alpha 1. */
    --color-variant-background: rgb({{ hz_variant_bg.rgb }});
    --color-variant-border: rgb({{ hz_variant_fg.rgb }});
    --color-variant-text: rgb({{ hz_variant_fg.rgb }});
    --color-variant-text-rgb: {{ hz_variant_fg.rgb }};
    --color-variant-hover-background: {{ hz_variant_hover_bg }};
    --color-variant-hover-text: rgb({{ hz_variant_hover_text.rgb }});
    --color-variant-hover-border: {{ hz_variant_hover_border }};

    --color-selected-variant-background: rgb({{ hz_variant_fg.rgb }});
    --color-selected-variant-border: rgb({{ hz_variant_fg.rgb }});
    --color-selected-variant-text: rgb({{ hz_variant_bg.rgb }});
    --color-selected-variant-hover-background: {{ hz_selected_hover_bg }};
    --color-selected-variant-hover-text: rgb({{ hz_selected_hover_text.rgb }});
    --color-selected-variant-hover-border: {{ hz_selected_hover_border }};

    /* Backdrop color as a SPACE triplet from scheme-1's shadow color.
       Horizon consumes rgb(var(--backdrop-color-rgb) / var(--backdrop-opacity))
       slash syntax (base.css:1163); Dawn's own --color-shadow is a COMMA
       triplet and CSS cannot convert between the formats (dual-format
       gotcha) — so the space triplet is emitted from Liquid here.
       Scheme-1-only caveat per --color-border above. */
    --color-shadow-rgb: {{ popover_scheme.settings.shadow.rgb }};

    /* --- Phase 13 (quick-add / buy-buttons subsystem; Horizon rem = 16px) --- */
    /* Font sizes (tsv:349, 352-353) */
    --font-size--3xs: 10px; /* 0.625rem */
    --font-size--sm: 14px; /* 0.875rem */
    --font-size--md: 16px; /* 1rem */

    /* Gaps (tsv:435, 438-439, 441) */
    --gap-2xs: 4.8px; /* 0.3rem */
    --gap-md: 14.4px; /* 0.9rem */
    --gap-lg: 16px; /* 1rem */
    --gap-2xl: 32px; /* 2rem */

    /* Animation timings (tsv:473, 489, 492 — verbatim) */
    --ease-out-cubic: cubic-bezier(0.33, 1, 0.68, 1);
    --animation-timing-bounce: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
    --animation-timing-fade-out: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);

    /* Buttons (tsv:582 verbatim px; tsv:648 verbatim calc — both calc deps
       already ported, Phases 5) */
    --button-size-md: 36px;
    --height-buy-buttons: calc(var(--padding-lg) * 2 + var(--icon-size-sm));

    /* Inputs (tsv:557-559; 0.8rem → 12.8px) — gift-card recipient form */
    --input-padding-y: 12.8px;
    --input-padding-x: 12.8px;
    --input-padding: var(--input-padding-y) var(--input-padding-x);

    /* Drawer (tsv:129 30rem; tsv:457 1rem; tsv:467 with drawer_border_color
       at its SCHEMA default = palette foreground — composed via rgb() from
       scheme-1 text per the --color-border precedent above; the
       .color-custom-drawer scope below re-declares --color-border full-color
       inside the drawer). */
    --theme-drawer-width: 480px; /* 30rem */
    --style-border-radius-lg: 16px; /* 1rem */
    --style-border-drawer: 1px solid rgb({{ popover_scheme.settings.text.rgb }});

    /* Quick-add modal geometry (tsv:666-668; rem→px @16 inside min()) */
    --quick-add-modal-height: min(616px, 96vh); /* 38.5rem */
    --quick-add-modal-width: min(864px, 96vw); /* 54rem */
    --quick-add-modal-gallery-width: 384px; /* 24rem */

    /* Button radii (tsv:460-461 at schema defaults
       button_border_radius_primary/_secondary = 100) — first consumers: the
       quantity-selector extraction's stepper radius legs. The BARE
       --style-border-radius-buttons (input radius, base.css:3031) is
       undefined in stock too — IACVT → 0, kept absent (Phase-13 audit-note
       precedent). */
    --style-border-radius-buttons-primary: 100px;
    --style-border-radius-buttons-secondary: 100px;

    /* Phase-13 audit notes — deliberately NOT defined:
       --color-foreground-secondary (buy-buttons-styles:58/69/256) is consumed
       but never defined anywhere in stock Horizon — stock behavior is the
       IACVT `color` fallback to inherited color; defining it here would
       deviate. --image-gap (quick-add-modal-styles:485) only feeds the
       .media-gallery__grid rule, which sits on the media-gallery markup this
       slice TRIMS from the quick-add modal — RE-ADD its source (block-settings
       inline style, product-media-gallery-content.liquid:353) with the PDP
       media slice. The --quick-add-display/-mobile-display/-mobile-opacity
       vars are GONE from card markup as of Phase 13 round 3 (Dawn-native
       quick-add — product-card.liquid no longer emits them); their only
       consumers sit in the unwired snippets/quick-add-styles. */
  }

  /* Section-height svh tiers (tsv:143-151, verbatim incl. Horizon's em
     breakpoints: 40em = 640px, 60em = 960px at browser-default 16px —
     media-query em ignores Dawn's 62.5% root font-size) */
  @media screen and (min-width: 40em) {
    :root {
      --section-height-small: 40svh;
      --section-height-medium: 55svh;
      --section-height-large: 70svh;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 60em) {
    :root {
      --section-height-small: 50svh;
      --section-height-medium: 65svh;
      --section-height-large: 80svh;
    }
  }

  /* Phase 10: responsive tiers (Horizon's own 750px query — px, unlike the
     em-based section-height queries above). Badge paddings tsv:540-543;
     card heights tsv:657-661 (rem->px @16). */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    :root {
      --badge-blob-padding-block: 4px;
      --badge-blob-padding-inline: 16px 12px;
      --badge-rectangle-padding-block: 4px;
      --badge-rectangle-padding-inline: 10px;

      --height-small: 280px; /* 17.5rem */
      --height-medium: 340px; /* 21.25rem */
      --height-large: 400px; /* 25rem */
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%}
  Phase 9: the .color-custom-popover scope (mirrors Horizon tsv:685-691 —
  this file IS our tsv analog; every host renders it, and popup-link is
  only reachable inside hosts). Emits FULL-COLOR --color-background /
  --color-foreground on .color-custom-popover, satisfying the dialog
  surface rules (snippets/dialog-styles.liquid + popup-link's verbatim
  background-color: var(--color-background)) with no dual-format fix.
  Inputs = Dawn scheme-1 background/text, exactly Horizon's popover
  setting defaults (palette background/foreground); border_color = text
  per the same defaults.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'contrast-override',
  background_color: popover_scheme.settings.background,
  text_color: popover_scheme.settings.text,
  border_color: popover_scheme.settings.text,
  section_id: 'popover',
  preset: 'ui'
%}

{%- comment -%}
  Phase 10: the .color-custom-badge-sale / -sold-out scopes (mirrors Horizon
  tsv:701-713 — the .color-custom-popover precedent above). Inputs = Horizon
  SCHEMA defaults mapped onto Dawn scheme-1: sale background = palette
  foreground (scheme-1 text; text_color omitted exactly like stock's
  default-less badge_sale_text_color — contrast-override picks the
  brightness-based extreme), sold-out background = palette background with
  foreground text.

  Phase 11: CONSUMER-LESS since the gallery's badge hardcode was replaced by
  the _product-badges block (which colors its spans with Dawn scheme classes
  instead — see its header). Kept deliberately: stock-parity tokens, tiny
  CSS, and the scopes come back into play if a stock-faithful
  .product-badges__badge consumer is ever re-added.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'contrast-override',
  background_color: popover_scheme.settings.text,
  section_id: 'badge-sale',
  preset: 'ui'
%}

{% render 'contrast-override',
  background_color: popover_scheme.settings.background,
  text_color: popover_scheme.settings.text,
  section_id: 'badge-sold-out',
  preset: 'ui'
